.TH "PR1889CLI\-UPGRADE" "1" "" "pr1889cli" "Dedalus Manual"
.SH "NAME"
pr1889cli\-upgrade \- upgrade pr1889cli to the latest release
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B pr1889cli upgrade
[\fB\-\-check\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Replaces this pr1889cli executable with the latest published release, after verifying the download against the checksums published alongside it.
.PP
When pr1889cli was installed through a package manager (Homebrew) nothing is replaced. That manager owns the installed files, and overwriting them leaves its database describing a file that is no longer there, so the command runs the manager's own upgrade command instead, with its output on this terminal.
.PP
pr1889cli also checks for a newer release at most once a day and mentions one on standard error. That check is skipped when either standard output or standard error is not a terminal, when CI is set, when running under sudo, and when NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER or PR1889CLI_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER is set in the environment.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Report the installed and latest versions and exit, without installing anything.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
The command completed successfully.
.TP
\fB1\fR
The command failed. The reason is reported on standard error.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command was invoked incorrectly (missing or invalid arguments).
.PP
When pr1889cli cannot perform the upgrade itself (a project dependency, a cache such as npx, a package manager it cannot find) it prints what to run instead and exits 0, having changed nothing. Run pr1889cli upgrade \-\-check first to learn whether a newer release exists.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR pr1889cli (1),
.BR pr1889cli\-uninstall (1)
